---
layout: changelog
title: "Flag, reject, and block breached passwords in Appwrite Auth"
date: 2026-09-29
cover: /images/blog/announcing-breached-password-detection/cover.avif
tags: auth, security
---

Appwrite Auth now checks passwords against the Have I Been Pwned breach corpus with [breached password detection](/docs/products/auth/security#breached-passwords). Every password a user signs up, signs in, or resets with is checked, and the result is stored on the user as `passwordPwned`. Only the first five characters of the password's SHA-1 hash leave Appwrite.

On Appwrite Cloud, checking and recording are on by default. From **Auth** > **Policies** > **Passwords** in the Console, you can also reject breached passwords at sign-up and password changes, and block sign-in with a breached password until the user resets it. Self-hosted instances on Appwrite 2.3 and later turn it on with the `_APP_PWNED_PASSWORDS_DSN` environment variable.

